The Concept: Figuring out how many people board a bus when there is a rolling line of waiting passengers and limited seats.
Skills Used: Recursive CTEs (WITH RECURSIVE), Window Functions, LEFT JOIN.

Used Recursive CTEs to build a system that tracks a moving queue of people waiting for buses based on chronological arrival times.
Calculated "leftover" passengers who couldn't fit on a full bus and mathematically carried that number forward to the next available bus.
Combined grouping logic and joins to clean and prep raw data into a timeline before running the recursive loop.
